# Original 14.7.50: exclusion of the alternating-seven component

The original local hypotheses construct the marked A₇/S₇ quotient and a
faithful irreducible quotient of the literal U_I/V₁ section. The complete
small-module catalogue retains four plus its dual until two source cubic
orbits exclude it. This supplies the genuine four-or-natural-six dichotomy.

In rank four the original seed normalizer is the even four-plus-three
partition stabilizer, whose cubic quotient contradicts the actual partial
inverter. For the natural module the original seed remains a transitive
binary plane. Simultaneous Sylow and module markings force its flag point
to have weight two or four; the source cubic span and centralizer-rank
contradictions exclude both. All lifting retains the full two-kernel.

`source_14_7_50_at` excludes A₇ at every original local component. The
RowExclusions and Data consumers discharge this row, retaining only the
independent linear, A₆, and G₂ exclusions and genuine earlier source inputs.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith 14.7.50, printed pp.1064–1065, refs/quasithin.pdf.
